 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Cleaning them with mild cleaner through the paint layer is safe. If you want go deeper, a little electronics cleaner is very gentle. That's nice, it gives them a little fresh paint breather. A thin coat builds up quickly. You can usually save them by soaking them in water overnight. If they' still stiff after that, they're beyond rescue and need to be replaced. Then fully dry them on a towel and use them while you can. If you start getting bad ones, it's time to switch brands.",
